WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.387 --> 00:00:18.028
Maggie, and Cole walked over to the picnic tables.

2
00:00:19.029 --> 00:00:21.991
People from a local restaurant were passing out snacks and drinks.

3
00:00:22.951 --> 00:00:26.733
Henry took a bottle of water, but he felt too worried to eat a snack.

4
00:00:27.514 --> 00:00:31.496
What if The Lemonade Detectives couldn't solve this case before the end of the ride?

5
00:00:33.576 --> 00:00:36.517
So far they'd done everything detectives were supposed to do.

6
00:00:37.718 --> 00:00:40.999
They'd figured out suspects, motives, and alibis.

7
00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:43.420
But they still hadn't solved the case.

8
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:49.002
"Let's split up and question our last two suspects," Henry told his friends.

9
00:00:49.022 --> 00:00:51.343
"Okay," Cole agreed.

10
00:00:51.363 --> 00:00:54.044
"I'll try to talk to the mystery man if you want."

11
00:00:54.064 --> 00:00:57.366
"Fine. Maggie and I will find William."

12
00:00:58.226 --> 00:01:00.027
They split up and started searching.

13
00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:03.048
The picnic area was crowded.

14
00:01:03.788 --> 00:01:06.549
At first Henry didn't see either of their suspects.

15
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:08.910
Then Maggie grabbed his arm.

16
00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.531
"There's William."

17
00:01:11.531 --> 00:01:13.492
Henry looked toward where she was pointing.

18
00:01:14.432 --> 00:01:18.794
William was sitting by himself, staring out at the woods and eating an apple.

19
00:01:18.814 --> 00:01:23.856
"Let's decide what we're going to say before we go over," Henry said.

20
00:01:23.876 --> 00:01:27.718
"We don't have time," Maggie said impatiently.

21
00:01:27.738 --> 00:01:30.799
"Let's just go tell him we know he did it.

22
00:01:31.399 --> 00:01:33.020
If he's guilty, he might confess."

23
00:01:34.068 --> 00:01:35.329
"I'm not sure that will work."

24
00:01:35.709 --> 00:01:37.010
Henry glanced at William.

25
00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.852
The new boy looked bored and lonely.

26
00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:44.455
Even though William was a suspect, Henry felt a little sorry for him.

27
00:01:45.476 --> 00:01:47.597
It couldn't be easy being the new kid in town.

28
00:01:47.617 --> 00:01:51.980
"Look, his bag is on the table behind him," Maggie said.

29
00:01:52.781 --> 00:01:54.042
"Come on, I have a plan!"

30
00:01:54.062 --> 00:01:55.342
"A plan?

31
00:01:55.743 --> 00:01:56.303
What is it?"

32
00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:57.664
Henry felt worried.

33
00:01:58.565 --> 00:02:03.248
Maggie wasn't usually the type of person who came up with logical, well-thought-out plans.

34
00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:08.569
She was the type of person who acted first and thought about it later.

35
00:02:08.589 --> 00:02:12.670
"There's no time to explain," Maggie said.

36
00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:16.451
"Just talk to him to distract him, and I'll take care of the rest."

37
00:02:16.471 --> 00:02:19.332
"Maggie, wait!"

38
00:02:19.692 --> 00:02:20.332
Henry said.

39
00:02:21.312 --> 00:02:22.293
It was too late.

40
00:02:22.953 --> 00:02:26.434
Maggie was already rushing toward the picnic table where William was sitting.

41
00:02:27.374 --> 00:02:31.175
Henry followed, hoping that her plan would work, whatever it was.

42
00:02:32.255 --> 00:02:34.036
William looked up when he saw them coming.

43
00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:37.381
He didn't look particularly happy to see them.

44
00:02:37.401 --> 00:02:40.983
"Hi," Henry said, trying to sound friendly.

45
00:02:41.003 --> 00:02:43.064
"That apple looks good.

46
00:02:43.825 --> 00:02:44.625
Where did you get it?"

47
00:02:45.526 --> 00:02:49.908
"Over there," William said, pointing to a basket that the restaurant people had set out.

48
00:02:49.928 --> 00:02:54.330
"Oh great Henry was running out of things to say.

49
00:02:55.071 --> 00:02:56.772
He shot a desperate look at Maggie.

50
00:02:58.473 --> 00:03:00.814
She flopped down on the bench across from William.

51
00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:04.436
"Whew!" she exclaimed dramatically.

52
00:03:05.308 --> 00:03:06.788
"I'm so tired!"

53
00:03:07.829 --> 00:03:09.069
She flung her arms out.

54
00:03:09.869 --> 00:03:13.050
One knocked into William's unzipped bag and sent it flying.

55
00:03:13.991 --> 00:03:15.771
The contents scattered everywhere.

56
00:03:15.791 --> 00:03:18.372
"Hey!" William exclaimed.

57
00:03:18.392 --> 00:03:20.732
"You spilled all my stuff!"

58
00:03:21.853 --> 00:03:24.974
"Sorry," Maggie said, leaping down and grabbing the bag.

59
00:03:26.294 --> 00:03:27.414
She shook it upside down.

60
00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:29.315
"Oops, you're right.

61
00:03:29.435 --> 00:03:30.415
Everything fell out!

62
00:03:31.035 --> 00:03:32.556
But don't worry, I'll clean it up."

63
00:03:33.536 --> 00:03:36.637
Henry and William watched as she picked up all the spilled items.

64
00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:41.238
There was a cell phone, a house key, and a few other things.

65
00:03:41.258 --> 00:03:44.739
"There." Maggie zipped the bag shut.

66
00:03:44.759 --> 00:03:46.020
"All fixed."

67
00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.600
"Thanks," William muttered.

68
00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.841
"Um, did you guys want to sit here, or what?"

69
00:03:51.861 --> 00:03:54.742
"Maybe later," Maggie said.

70
00:03:54.762 --> 00:03:56.102
"Come on, Henry.

71
00:03:56.142 --> 00:03:57.163
Let's go find Cole."

72
00:04:00.004 --> 00:04:01.384
The two of them made their escape.

73
00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:04.981
"What was that all about?"

74
00:04:05.321 --> 00:04:07.983
Henry asked as soon as they were out of William's earshot.

75
00:04:09.004 --> 00:04:09.985
Maggie smiled.

76
00:04:10.005 --> 00:04:11.406
"Don't you get it?

77
00:04:12.907 --> 00:04:16.269
There was nothing in that bag that William could have used to slash the tires.

78
00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:23.014
And his bike shorts don't have pockets, so he couldn't be carrying a penknife or anything that way."

79
00:04:23.034 --> 00:04:26.476
"I suppose you're right," Henry agreed.

80
00:04:26.496 --> 00:04:31.940
"But how do you know he didn't drop the crime weapon in the woods after he used it?"

81
00:04:33.428 --> 00:04:34.549
Maggie's face fell.

82
00:04:34.569 --> 00:04:36.610
"I didn't think of that."

83
00:04:36.991 --> 00:04:37.611
She frowned.

84
00:04:37.631 --> 00:04:40.453
"Why do you always have to be so logical?"

85
00:04:40.473 --> 00:04:41.974
"Never mind.

86
00:04:42.775 --> 00:04:45.256
It was still a pretty good plan," Henry said.

87
00:04:45.276 --> 00:04:49.219
"If there had been a penknife in there, it would've worked."

88
00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:50.900
"That's true."

89
00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:52.882
Maggie looked a little happier.

90
00:04:52.902 --> 00:04:56.484
"So should we go back and try to talk to William some more?"

91
00:04:57.425 --> 00:05:01.928
Before Henry could answer, he saw Cole rushing toward them, looking excited.

92
00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:03.641
"Big news!"

93
00:05:04.141 --> 00:05:05.402
he cried when he reached them.

94
00:05:05.422 --> 00:05:07.743
"Did you talk to the mystery man?"

95
00:05:08.083 --> 00:05:08.863
Henry asked.

96
00:05:09.844 --> 00:05:10.784
Cole shook his head.

97
00:05:10.805 --> 00:05:13.766
"I never found him," he said breathlessly.

98
00:05:13.786 --> 00:05:16.988
"But I did find out more about him.

99
00:05:17.568 --> 00:05:18.669
And about William too."

100
00:05:18.689 --> 00:05:21.010
"Really?" Maggie said.

101
00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.291
"Like what?"

102
00:05:22.311 --> 00:05:26.333
"Like William's family isn't just rich," Cole said.

103
00:05:26.353 --> 00:05:29.334
"His dad works for the government.

104
00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:32.076
He's a senator in the United States Senate!"

105
00:05:33.564 --> 00:05:35.026
"Really?" Henry said.

106
00:05:36.187 --> 00:05:37.309
"Wow. That's cool."

107
00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:39.011
Cole nodded.

108
00:05:39.031 --> 00:05:41.173
"But that's not all," he said.

109
00:05:41.193 --> 00:05:45.899
"Everyone has noticed that the mystery man follows William everywhere.

110
00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.904
What if he's planning to kidnap William and hold him for ransom?"
